        <p>Even the Tories themselves are now ming to spesk disrespectfully of and even to tile their owl legislation. Mr. Gamine ITRDRIr thinks that if the principle embodied me Merzhandiee Marks Act be carried much her we shall " be marked out of house and iv,' and Mr. LOWTHER incidentally established fact that the pencils supplied to the House of mons are marked" Made in Bavaria." Disco.- sot ths sort should do large amount of good. y help to bring home to the minds of people fact that nn inunensd amount of harm may be shy ignorant md injoil,chms rneddhisg with course of trade. Sir HOWARD VINCINT is now ions to provide that instead ol the words"Msde ermany,"iir "Medal° Itelgium,"being 0.0(1 on imported articles some such words lie .1 °reign le " should be subetituted. This, he seems to ik, will deprive the German or the Belgian of pecial advertisement, while customers will still stile to discriminate between the foreign and homemade article. Mr. RITCHIZ, however, ng on liehalf of the Goverment, would not is anything to do with Sir Ma'am, VINORNTR but he intimated that some inquiry might be le into the working of the Merchandise Mork. . If that Act is doing the mischief which is ged against it the sooner this inquiry is held better it will be.</p>
