        <p>Col•tetow finnan Rowan+ HMO.. About 5-30 on Monday ownt the amasser Towle, of Ballast, Ireland, and the taa York, were in Onilision in OS. Rhin Canal undo, Runcorn Swage. The tug renamed tame abet darri•ge, and prneseded to the Old Quay for repairs. The ft ern. woe dtmaaed on the port inde, but it proceeded on Its Journey. • twang tide tau running St the time. _</p>
        <p>B.or AMITAVTA. BALL.</p>
        <p>The fifth annual bell in concretion with the Runcorn Shop Assistants Amsmiation wee held on W. &amp;swim, evening in the Public Ilse. Runcorn. The room had been beautifully no toed by Mr. Leech. A caplsl programme cdnsleting of 24 dances was submit`ed and was thoroughly enjoyed. Mr. P,•••••11'4 bend eupplied the mimic. whilst the red reshromit bar was teenaged by Mn. C. Dutton of the Wileon's Rotel. IfnuytStne.nCu OM All OM 0 . On Thursday morning. before Mn. F. J. Norman, and I Mr. H. Taylor. at the Runcorn Police Court, glimbeth Harker, an old offender was committed to inutsford Primo, for two months with hard labour for eleeping out in Egerton-street, early that morning—Mr. Norman in senteacing her to the above mentronel terns of im- prisonment, remarked that she had given both the police and magietratee. end's. of trouble. Ho warned her that she would be morn eeverelv dealt with if eke appeared again before,that cane.</p>
